Thought: I'll first generate a list of oxide compositions and retrieve their polymorphs using batch retrieval. I'll focus on binary oxides for simplicity.
Action: batch_retrieve_polymorphs
Action Input: {"compositions": ["Al2O3", "TiO2", "ZnO", "CuO", "Fe2O3", "MgO", "NiO", "CoO", "MnO2", "Cr2O3", "V2O5", "WO3", "MoO3", "Ta2O5", "Nb2O5", "HfO2", "ZrO2", "SnO2", "PbO", "Bi2O3"], "max_energy_above_hull": 0.3, "max_per_composition": 3, "save_directory": "oxide_polymorphs"}

Thought: Great! We've successfully retrieved polymorphs for all 20 oxide compositions. Now we need to consolidate these individual files into a single dataset and prepare it for ML training.
Action: consolidate_polymorph_datasets
Action Input: {"composition_files": {"Al2O3": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/Al2O3_polymorphs.json", "TiO2": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/TiO2_polymorphs.json", "ZnO": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/ZnO_polymorphs.json", "CuO": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/CuO_polymorphs.json", "Fe2O3": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/Fe2O3_polymorphs.json", "MgO": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/MgO_polymorphs.json", "NiO": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/NiO_polymorphs.json", "CoO": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/CoO_polymorphs.json", "MnO2": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/MnO2_polymorphs.json", "Cr2O3": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/Cr2O3_polymorphs.json", "V2O5": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/V2O5_polymorphs.json", "WO3": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/WO3_polymorphs.json", "MoO3": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/MoO3_polymorphs.json", "Ta2O5": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/Ta2O5_polymorphs.json", "Nb2O5": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/Nb2O5_polymorphs.json", "HfO2": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/HfO2_polymorphs.json", "ZrO2": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/ZrO2_polymorphs.json", "SnO2": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/SnO2_polymorphs.json", "PbO": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/PbO_polymorphs.json", "Bi2O3": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/oxide_polymorphs/Bi2O3_polymorphs.json"}, "output_path": "consolidated_oxides.json"}

Thought: Now that we have consolidated the data, let's prepare it for ML training using the prepare_tabular_dataset tool with advanced feature engineering and the specified parameters.
Action: prepare_tabular_dataset
Action Input: {"polymorphs_json_path": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/consolidated_oxides.json", "output_path": "ml_dataset", "target_property": "formation_energy_per_atom", "feature_engineering": "advanced", "test_split": 0.2, "normalize": true}

Thought: Now that we have prepared the dataset, let's train the XGBoost model using the specified hyperparameters from the input data.
Action: train_xgboost_model
Action Input: {"train_data_path": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/ml_dataset/train.csv", "test_data_path": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/ml_dataset/test.csv", "model_save_path": "xgboost_model.pkl", "target_column": "formation_energy_per_atom", "hyperparameters": {"n_estimators": 200, "max_depth": 8, "learning_rate": 0.1, "subsample": 0.8, "colsample_bytree": 0.8, "reg_alpha": 0.1, "reg_lambda": 0.1}}

Thought: Let's perform cross-validation to get a more robust estimate of model performance, and then combine all evaluation results into the required JSON format.
Action: perform_cross_validation
Action Input: {"train_data_path": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_oxides_trial_0/ml_dataset/train.csv", "target_column": "formation_energy_per_atom", "cv_folds": 5, "hyperparameters": {"n_estimators": 200, "max_depth": 8, "learning_rate": 0.1, "subsample": 0.8, "colsample_bytree": 0.8, "reg_alpha": 0.1, "reg_lambda": 0.1}}

Thought: Now I'll combine all the evaluation results into the required JSON format and save it to a file.
Action: write_file
